Remove five Postfix settings that no code path reaches. `tls_high_cipherlist`, `tls_preempt_cipherlist` and `smtpd_tls_session_cache_database` have had no effect since server-side TLS moved to nginx in 2017 -- Postfix's `smtpd` offers no TLS of its own, so none of the three is ever read. `postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol` and the `smtpd pass` service in `master.cf` are leftovers of the postscreen setup that was reverted a week after it landed in 2023. No behaviour changes.
